# PCBZ wasm page patch 0011: the page's own project route across the WebAssembly boundary.
# Why: the PCBZ page runs upstream's browser editor (apps/pcbcraft-web, eframe on a canvas) inside the
# product pane. The host must load and save the session's .pcbz through the plugin's routes instead of
# the browser's file dialog and download UI. The editor already has one browser edge for each: pickProject
# (a file input) and downloadProject (an anchor download) in crates/app/src/project_files/web.rs. This patch
# keeps both as the plain-browser fallback and, when the host page provides globalThis.pcbzHostPick /
# globalThis.pcbzOnSave, routes through those instead. A small queue in the new crates/app/src/host.rs is
# drained at the start of the editor frame: load goes through ProjectFiles::open -> web::open_bytes (the
# same validation, decoding and migration as an upload), save through ProjectFiles::save (the same encoder,
# unchanged-byte reuse and upgrade notices as a download), and a command through PcbApp::run (the same path
# as a menu item), so the editor itself is unchanged. The exports live in the web runner, not in the app
# library, so a binary's wasm-bindgen glue carries them as it already carries pcbcraft_fill_worker.
# Functions touched: project_files/web.rs pickProject/setUnsaved/downloadProject (inline JS guards),
# web::open split into open + open_bytes; project_files.rs ProjectFiles::open_host added; lib.rs host_tick
# and its call at the top of frame_inner, pub mod host; new host.rs; apps/pcbcraft-web/src/main.rs exports
# pcbz_host_open, pcbz_host_save, pcbz_host_command, pcbz_host_status.

